# The revision, literally [revised version](https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/revision), The revision most often refers to a commit object in Git, or a revision number in SVN.
#
# `head` refers to where you are right now; the current reference at a
# given time.The revision can be a full [hash value (see
# glossary)](https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/FIPS/NIST.FIPS.186-5.pdf),
# of the recorded change to a ref within a repository pointing to a
# commit [commit](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-commit) object. It does
# not necessarily have to be a hash; it can simply define a [revision
# number](https://svnbook.red-bean.com/en/1.7/svn.tour.revs.specifiers.html)
# which is an integer that is monotonically increasing. In cases where
# it is identical to the `ref.head.name`, it SHOULD still be included.
# It is up to the implementer to decide which value to set as the
# revision based on the VCS system and situational context.
#
# @note Stability Level: release_candidate
#
# pkg:gem/opentelemetry-semantic_conventions#lib/opentelemetry/semconv/incubating/vcs/attributes.rb:117
OpenTelemetry::SemConv::Incubating::VCS::VCS_REF_HEAD_REVISION = T.let(T.unsafe(nil), String)

# The type of the [reference](https://git-scm.com/docs/gitglossary#def_ref) in the repository.
#
# `head` refers to where you are right now; the current reference at a
# given time.
#
# @note Stability Level: release_candidate
#
# pkg:gem/opentelemetry-semantic_conventions#lib/opentelemetry/semconv/incubating/vcs/attributes.rb:125
OpenTelemetry::SemConv::Incubating::VCS::VCS_REF_HEAD_TYPE = T.let(T.unsafe(nil), String)

# The number of lines added/removed in a ref (branch) relative to the ref from the `vcs.ref.base.name` attribute.
#
# This metric should be reported for each `vcs.line_change.type` value. For example if a ref added 3 lines and removed 2 lines,
# instrumentation SHOULD report two measurements: 3 and 2 (both positive numbers).
# If number of lines added/removed should be calculated from the start of time, then `vcs.ref.base.name` SHOULD be set to an empty string.
#
# @note Stability Level: release_candidate
#
# pkg:gem/opentelemetry-semantic_conventions#lib/opentelemetry/semconv/incubating/vcs/metrics.rb:64
OpenTelemetry::SemConv::Incubating::VCS::VCS_REF_LINES_DELTA = T.let(T.unsafe(nil), String)

# The number of revisions (commits) a ref (branch) is ahead/behind the branch from the `vcs.ref.base.name` attribute.
#
# This metric should be reported for each `vcs.revision_delta.direction` value. For example if branch `a` is 3 commits behind and 2 commits ahead of `trunk`,
# instrumentation SHOULD report two measurements: 3 and 2 (both positive numbers) and `vcs.ref.base.name` is set to `trunk`.
#
# @note Stability Level: release_candidate
#
# pkg:gem/opentelemetry-semantic_conventions#lib/opentelemetry/semconv/incubating/vcs/metrics.rb:72
OpenTelemetry::SemConv::Incubating::VCS::VCS_REF_REVISIONS_DELTA = T.let(T.unsafe(nil), String)

# Time a ref (branch) created from the default branch (trunk) has existed. The `ref.type` attribute will always be `branch`.
